DOC=store-persist run rebuilds, once a day, a database's durable copy once it exceeds this percentage of the live store's size: a backup never sheds chunks the live store has collected, and a reboot restores the whole copy into RAM.
SCHEMA=Percentage of the live store's size past which the daily rebuild in store-persist run rebuilds a durable copy (default 150; at least 100).
